notes:
•  NEW: Sound. You hear the camera of the active tile (the one you clicked) - its name bar shows a speaker:
     - live tiles play the camera's microphone as it happens;
     - tiles in playback play the recording's sound in step with the picture at 1x to 4x (faster sounds higher, like a tape); above 4x, backwards, paused or while dragging the timeline it's silent;
     - click the speaker on a tile's name bar to mute just that camera (crossed out in red; remembered);
     - toolbar: speaker button = all sound on/off (Ctrl+M), slider = volume. Both apply instantly and are remembered.
     Only cameras with a microphone or audio module, with sound switched on in the camera, give sound.
